  "subtitle": "This month's VMA goes to [LINK:1963:JIM_99_thor0|JIM #99], where we find Jane Foster, having just witnessed Don Blake getting thrown out of an upper-story window - the caption reads \"And then, because she <i>is</i> a female...\" Hyde says, \"She <i>fainted</i>!\"&nbsp; <i>OMG</i>!",
  "review_text": "Not a stellar month for Marvel, with 8 graded stories spread out over 6 books (both Amazing Spider-Man and Strange Tales had two), averaging only a middling 4.08, which is just barely at \"reader\" level.&nbsp; The <i>Strange Tales</i> #116, in particular, dragged the average down by over half a point (as far as I'm concerned, Doctor Strange is still a no-show) - let's face it - Marvel did little this month to provide quality to its readers above just an average <i>Meh</i> rating.\n\nOn the positive side were the crossovers (though Spider-Man crashing Johnny's party was ghastly and should never have been done) and the appearance by the Watcher.&nbsp; And the main story from ASM was solid, as was the FF issue, but they were only around mid-grade, so nothing earth-shattering.\n\n\n\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** SUMMARY_BEGIN ***\n*** THIS MONTH ***0 graded stories over 0 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 0 grade character issue weight0.00*** LAST MONTH ***9 graded stories over 8 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 6.58 grade character issue   weight 6.0   asm       ASM #7  1.00 5.5   strange   ST #115 0.33 5.0   thor      JIM #98 0.50 5.0   giant     TTA #50 0.50 5.0   torch     ST #115 0.50 5.0   iron      TOS #48 0.75 4.0   ff        FF #21  1.00 3.0   xmen      XMEN #2 1.00 1.5   aven      AVEN #2 1.004.19\n*** SUMMARY_END ***]",
  "letters_page": "[HANG0] * Introduction of Mr. Hyde\n[HANG0] * Peter Parker punching Flash Thompson in the boxing ring\n[HANG0] * Sue Storm finally getting some offensive powers\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** INTRODUCTION_BEGIN ***\n*** INTRODUCTION_END ***]\n\n<b>Roundup:</b>\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_BEGIN ***]\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_END ***]",
  "ownership": "[HANG0] * Sub-Mariner wanders into the Avengers sphere of influence\n[HANG0] * Thor finishes things up with Mr. Hyde\n[HANG0] * A \"Black Knight\" shows up to menace Giant-Man and the Wasp\n[HANG0] * The X-Men face a huge blob of an enemy\n[HANG0] * Spider-Man faces a \"shocking\" new foe\n[HANG0] * The Human Torch gets a second crack at a slippery foe\n[HANG0] * Dr. Doom is back once again\n[HANG0] * and Iron Man faces some dude wearing a <i>bunch</i> of rings!"
